From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS (1000), checker's fix: reads that are written back take memory's bytes, not the guard's copies

Port of yuri2301/Eglantine c5145ace9 (yuri2301, "frame overlap copies"); the defect below is in
upstream's version too.

Why: with 1000 on, every block read of a page with a frame-in-flight copy gets the copy's bytes
(the presented frame's), and GetSpan refuses such a range. Several GPU-side writers read the
destination first and write the whole range back (read-modify-write):
 - GuestMemoryScoped with a Write flag (DMA engine copies, upload engine, sw blitter, texture
   write-back's UnsafeReadWrite, buffer cache): Read() reads by block when there is no span, and
   the destructor writes the whole buffer back; a write-only range with its span refused writes
   back a buffer it never read;
 - the DMA engine's block-to-pitch stripes (StripeBlockToPitch);
 - the texture write-back's bands, tail and verify (TrySwizzleLayerInBands) and the copy form.
There the copy's bytes went back over memory: what the game wrote since the present (the reason
the page has a copy) was undone, in the bytes the GPU write did not cover (padding, other
columns, the tail).

Fix: a thread-local PlainReads scope (src/common/ahead_guard_plain.h) under which Overlay does
nothing (no copy over the read, no span refused). Held by GuestMemory::Read and the write-only
constructor when FLAGS has Write, by the DMA stripe's destination read, and through
TrySwizzleLayerInBands and SwizzleLayerCopyForm.

Off (EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS unset): a thread-local count up and down around those reads,
nothing else. No translation id input touched (guest_memory.h, maxwell_dma.cpp,
texture_cache/util.cpp, ahead_guard.h, the new common header). KEEPS THE STORE.
---
diff --git a/src/common/ahead_guard_plain.h b/src/common/ahead_guard_plain.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c8565434c8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/common/ahead_guard_plain.h
@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+#pragma once
+
+#include "common/common_types.h"
+
+// 1001 (checker's fix on 1000, EDEN_UP_AHEAD_GUARD_ALL_READS): while a PlainReads scope is up on
+// a thread, its block reads and spans of guest memory take memory's bytes, never the frame-ahead
+// guard's copies (video_core/ahead_guard.h, Overlay). For reads whose bytes are written back to
+// guest memory (a read-modify-write: GuestMemoryScoped with a Write flag, the DMA engine's
+// block-to-pitch stripes, the texture write-back's bands and tail): a copy there would write the
+// presented frame's bytes over what the game wrote since. Off: a thread-local count only.
+namespace Common::AheadGuardPlain {
+
+inline thread_local u32 depth = 0;
+
+struct PlainReads {
+    PlainReads() {
+        ++depth;
+    }
+    ~PlainReads() {
+        --depth;
+    }
+    PlainReads(const PlainReads&) = delete;
+    PlainReads& operator=(const PlainReads&) = delete;
+};
+
+/// A PlainReads scope when `on` (a Write range's read; see GuestMemory::Read).
+struct PlainReadsIf {
+    explicit PlainReadsIf(bool on_) : on{on_} {
+        if (on) {
+            ++depth;
+        }
+    }
+    ~PlainReadsIf() {
+        if (on) {
+            --depth;
+        }
+    }
+    PlainReadsIf(const PlainReadsIf&) = delete;
+    PlainReadsIf& operator=(const PlainReadsIf&) = delete;
+    const bool on;
+};
+
+inline bool Active() {
+    return depth != 0;
+}
+
+} // namespace Common::AheadGuardPlain
